Model replies: OpenAI gpt-4.1-mini-2025-04-14
https://openai.com/policies/services-agreement/

What is here from it. The agent and the user simulator both called this model through
OpenAI's API. The stored episodes contain every request sent and every reply received,
with the identifiers the API returned for each reply (a response id and a backend
fingerprint). No model weights are included.

The OpenAI Services Agreement, as published at the address above (marked "Updated:
December 1, 2025" when read on 2026-11-25), says of content sent to and received from
the API:

  "As between Customer and OpenAI, to the extent permitted by applicable law, Customer:
  (a) retains all ownership rights in Input; and (b) owns all Output. OpenAI hereby
  assigns to Customer all OpenAI’s right, title, and interest, if any, in and to Output."

That is the public text of the agreement. The terms on the account that made these calls
were not separately reviewed for this notice.

